---
// Copy set by Vikrant 30 Sep 2026. Both videos tell the gated-incident story; never reuse them for Atlas Flow.
// Primary action: the ~14 min walkthrough. Second: the Medium essay with its date.
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import { formatDate, writing } from "../../data/profile";

const essay = writing.find((p) => p.url.includes("ai-proposes-a-human-authorizes"));
---

<Base title="Incident-AI · the gated path">
  <h1>Incident-AI: the AI proposes, a human approves</h1>
  <p>Alert in → persist → proposal → human gate → traces. Drafts start unsent. Close needs a person.</p>
  <p class="primary"><a href="https://youtu.be/j048FYXrRqs">Watch the walkthrough (~14 min)</a></p>
  {essay && (
    <p>
      <a href={essay.url}>Read the essay on Medium: “{essay.title}”</a>
      <time class="muted" datetime={essay.date}> · {formatDate(essay.date)}</time>
    </p>
  )}
  <p><a href="https://youtu.be/z1tyxIPBWpM">Short clip: model down, ticket survives (~3 min)</a></p>
  <p><a href="/reliability/#incident-desk">See it handle this site's real incidents, live →</a></p>
  <p><a href="/notes/postmortem-game-day-1/">Postmortem: game day 1</a>, where I broke the site on purpose and it raised and triaged the incident.</p>
  <p class="muted">The model only proposes. Since 1 Oct 2026, every AI priority on the live desk waits for a human approval (the one earlier ticket is labelled with the rule it ran under), and AI priority never pages anyone: paging comes from an outside probe on this site's SLO.</p>
  <p>Code: <a href="https://github.com/vikiscoding/vikrant_perswebsite_incidents_aiengine">vikiscoding/vikrant_perswebsite_incidents_aiengine</a></p>
  <p class="muted">Scope: a Python engine running one site's incidents, not ServiceNow.</p>
</Base>

<style>
  .primary { font-size: 1.0625rem; font-weight: 600; margin-top: 1.25rem; }
</style>
